# Graphics hardware these machines do not have and cannot acquire. Both products
# drive an Adreno -- el2 an X1E80100, handheld a CQ8725S -- and neither is
# expected to drive an external GPU.
#
# amdgpu is one of the largest modules in the tree, so this is mostly a build
# time and image size win rather than a runtime one. The display-core and
# per-generation sub-options (DRM_AMD_DC, DC_FP, RADEON_USERPTR, HSA_AMD) depend
# on these and fall out on their own.
# CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_RADEON is not set

# The rest of AMD's platform support, which is x86-laptop or AMD-server silicon:
# ACP is the audio coprocessor on AMD APUs, XGBE the 10G MAC on AMD Seattle.
# CONFIG_SND_SOC_AMD_ACP is not set
# CONFIG_AMD_XGBE is not set

# The rest of the discrete/virtual GPU drivers, none of which can appear here.
# NOUVEAU is the other large one; AST and QXL are server BMC and SPICE virtual
# display adapters, VMWGFX a VMware guest driver. These kernels run on bare
# metal Qualcomm hardware, not as guests.
# CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_AST is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_QXL is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_VMWGFX is not set
